  },
  "prompts": {
   "turn1": "Summarise the unpaid invoices in invoices.md.",
   "turn2": "Thanks. For this one, could you redo it as one comma-separated line per invoice? I'm pasting it straight into a spreadsheet import. And what's the total outstanding?"
  },
  "answers": {
   "turn1": "There are 3 unpaid invoices, totalling **3,135.50 EUR**.\n\n| Invoice | Client | Amount | Due | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| INV-2042 | Moth & Lantern Books | 380.50 EUR | 2026-10-31 | **Overdue** (2 days, as of 2026-11-02) |\n| INV-2043 | Pellow Cycles | 2,115.00 EUR | 2026-11-10 | Due in 8 days |\n| INV-2044 | Quarrystone Bakery | 640.00 EUR | 2026-11-20 | Due in 18 days |\n\n- **Overdue:** INV-2042 is 380.50 EUR and is the only invoice past its due date.\n- **Largest:** INV-2043 is 2,115.00 EUR, which is about 67% of the unpaid total.\n- **Paid:** INV-2041 and INV-2045 are paid, so I left them out.",
   "turn2": "```\nnumber,client,amount,currency,due,status\nINV-2042,Moth & Lantern Books,380.50,EUR,2026-10-31,unpaid\nINV-2043,Pellow Cycles,2115.00,EUR,2026-11-10,unpaid\nINV-2044,Quarrystone Bakery,640.00,EUR,2026-11-20,unpaid\n```\n\nI removed the thousands separator from 2,115.00 so it doesn't split into two columns on import. I also moved the currency into its own column. Delete the first line if your import doesn't expect a header.\n\n**Total outstanding: 3,135.50 EUR** (380.50 + 2,115.00 + 640.00)."
  },
